; bfsodium PBKDF2_HMAC_SHA_256 : RFC 8018 section 5 2  and SP 800_132
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The pseudorandom function is sha256/hmac  PASTED  and
; entered once per ITERATION  not once per block; the block counter and the
; iteration count are both stepped by chacha20/add32  PASTED  and the
; accumulating exclusive or is chacha20/xor32  PASTED;
;
; As in sha256/hashcore  a run of ONE repeated token is a repetition rather
; than a decision and is written as such; every offset and every branch below
; was worked out from the map and written down;
;
; IO  in:  klen{2} LE  saltlen{2} LE  dklen{2} LE  c{4} LE
;          pwbuf{256}  saltbuf{256}
;     out: dk{dklen}
;
; Only the first klen bytes of the password buffer are looked at  and the
; first saltlen of the salt; the rest MUST be nought;
;
;   T{i} = U{1} xor U{2} xor and so on as far as U{c}
;   U{1} = PRF( password  salt then i as four bytes big endian )
;   U{j} = PRF( password  U{j minus 1} )
;
; THIS ONE NEEDS THE SLIDE THAT THE TWO SP 800_108 FILES DO NOT; the block
; counter belongs AFTER the salt  whose length is only known at run time  so
; the four bytes are dropped on the top of an empty message buffer and the
; whole buffer slides down until they are where they belong; the salt is then
; ADDED underneath  which cannot disturb them because its bytes beyond its own
; length are nought; That is sha256/hkdf's mechanism and it is used here for
; sha256/hkdf's reason;
;
; THE SLIDE IS CHEAP HERE AND IT IS WORTH SAYING WHY; it happens once per
; OUTPUT BLOCK and the hash happens c times per output block  so at any
; iteration count a caller would actually choose the slide is not measurable;
;
; ONE SUBTRACTION IS AN ADDITION; the iteration count comes down by one each
; turn  and a thirty two bit borrow written out here would be a fourth hand
; rolled carry; chacha20/add32 DROPS ITS FINAL CARRY  so adding 0xffffffff is
; subtracting one  and the count is stepped by the same proved adder that
; steps the block counter;
;
; T IS CLEARED AT THE HEAD OF EACH BLOCK  so the first iteration needs no
; special case: T exclusive or U{1} with T at nought is U{1};
;
; SALTLEN IS AT MOST A HUNDRED AND EIGHTY EIGHT  which is a hundred and ninety
; two less the four counter bytes; a hundred and ninety two is the most
; sha256/hmac takes from memory;
;
; C IS THIRTY TWO BITS AND THE ROUTINE IS CORRECT FOR ANY OF THEM  but only
; the smallest can be RUN; one iteration of this file costs 5203749719
; instructions  MEASURED as the difference between a run at c of one and a run
; at c of two  so RFC 6070's four thousand and ninety six is twenty one
; million million  which is days; The vectors therefore stop at c of two  and
; that is a limit on what can be demonstrated rather than on what the file
; does; the loop is the same code at every count;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  klen{2}     u16 LE  the password's length
;   @0x002:0x003  saltlen{2}  u16 LE  the salt's length
;   @0x004:0x005  dklen{2}    u16 LE  how many bytes are wanted
;   @0x006:0x009  c{4}        u32 LE  the iteration count  as given; KEPT
;   @0x00a:0x109  pwbuf{256}  u8      the password  as given
;   @0x10a:0x209  saltbuf{256} u8     the salt  as given
;   @0x20c:0x30b  ptemp{256}  u8      hands the password back after a copy
;   @0x30c:0x40b  stemp{256}  u8      hands the salt back after a copy
;   @0x410:0x422  the block counter's adder; add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x410
;                 its a{4} IS THE BLOCK COUNTER i  little endian
;   @0x424:0x427  ctmp{4}     hands the block counter back after a copy
;   @0x428:0x43a  the iteration count's adder; add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x428
;                 its a{4} IS THIS BLOCK'S COUNT  counted down by adding
;                 0xffffffff to it
;   @0x43c:0x43f  ctmp2{4}    hands c back after a copy
;   @0x440        the slide count  two hundred and fifty two less saltlen
;   @0x444:0x44b  owedlo owedhi chances flag test back and two spare cells
;   @0x44c        the flag that says another iteration is owed
;   @0x450:0x46f  T{32}       the accumulating exclusive or; written out and
;                             spent by the emit  and cleared for each block
;   @0x474:0x493  U{32}       the block the hash just made
;   @0x498:0x4b0  the exclusive or frame; xor32 footprint 0:25 at @0x498
;   @0x4b8:0xbc3  sha256/hmac's frame  pasted at @0x4b8; footprint 0:1803
;
; U IS SPENT EXACTLY ONCE; one token carries each of its bytes BOTH into the
; message buffer  where it is the next iteration's message  AND into the
; exclusive or's right operand; so it is not copied twice and not handed back;
;
; THE COUNT STILL OWED IS KEPT WHERE IT IS TESTED; dklen arrives at @0x004 and
; moves into the counts frame before the first block;
;
; Nothing buffers the output; each T is written as it is made and the last is
; cut short;
;
; A digest is a byte string and hmac leaves its answer as eight little endian
; words  so the copy into U reverses each word;

; read the three lengths  the iteration count and the two buffers
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
